Considered the ideologue of Puigcercós, the head of Innovació took for granted that the leader will be endorsed "in a change of various objectives."
And he listed five, of which two stand out.
The first is to "recompose" the executive to represent at least 90 per cent of militancy, i.e. to include new faces coming from Carod's related sector.
The second can be the great novelty.
Huguet proposes that ERC settlembler as an operating mechanism at once.
Thus, it calls for a reform of the statutes that will make it possible to hold congresses through delegates elected by suffrage.
Finishing the assembly model, an exception in the system of Spanish matches, has been an obsession of Puigcercó's team, which has already batted in this regard at the last two congresses.
In fact, the convulsive conclave of 2008 left the mandate to the management to review the assembly at a specific congress for the reform of statutes.
This appointment is still pending, as the inner tide of recent years discouraged itself from dealing with the matter.
"Now, with no sectors critical luxury, it can be a good time to retake it again and try to close it forever.
